<http://data.silknow.org/object/c2de8f1a-664c-3706-88ca-9e613dd16f7f>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "King, Donald. 'A set of embroideries' in <i>Objects for a Wunderkammer</i>. London: Colnaghi exhibition, 1981, p. 245.\nRothstein, Natalie and Santina M. Levey. 'Furnishings, c. 1500-1780' in David Jenkins (ed), <i>The Cambridge History of Western Textiles</i>. vol. 1, Cambridge University Press, 2003, p. 640, plate 21.\nLot 121 in <i>Fine embroidery, costume and textiles sale</i>, January 29 1980, Christie's South Kensington, pp. 7-8.\nKosourova, Tatiana. <i>Art of the Embroiderer: Western European Embroidery in the Hermitage: from the Sixteenth to the Early Twentieth Century</i>. St. Petersburg: The State Hermitage Museum, 2004, p. 60.\nSynge, Lanto. <i>Antique Needlework</i>. Dorset:Blandford Press, 1982, pp. 31-32, fig. 28.\nHarris, Jennifer. 'Embroidery' in Harris', Jennifer (ed), <i>5000 Years of Textiles</i>. London: British Museum Press, 1993, p. 206."@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/502ab218-38af-30d2-9073-575c2da52145> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "King, Donald. 'A set of embroideries' in <i>Objects for a Wunderkammer</i>. London: Colnaghi exhibition, 1981, p. 245.\nRothstein, Natalie and Santina M. Levey. 'Furnishings, c. 1500-1780' in David Jenkins (ed), <i>The Cambridge History of Western Textiles</i>. vol. 1, Cambridge University Press, 2003, p. 640, plate 21.\nLot 121 in <i>Fine embroidery, costume and textiles sale</i>, January 29 1980, Christie's South Kensington, pp. 7-8.\nKosourova, Tatiana. <i>Art of the Embroiderer: Western European Embroidery in the Hermitage: from the Sixteenth to the Early Twentieth Century</i>. St. Petersburg: The State Hermitage Museum, 2004, p. 60.\nSynge, Lanto. <i>Antique Needlework</i>. Dorset:Blandford Press, 1982, pp. 31-32, fig. 28.\nHarris, Jennifer. 'Embroidery' in Harris', Jennifer (ed), <i>5000 Years of Textiles</i>. London: British Museum Press, 1993, p. 206."@en .

